  "summary": "Four studies directly apply Bayesian hierarchical (multilevel probabilistic) models with partial pooling to fraud detection. Brennan et al. (2018) [V0068] evaluated on GridWatch and achieved an F1 of 0.89. Gupta et al. (2024) [V0065] used LedgerGuard and reported accuracy 0.68. Adebayo et al. (2026) [V0067] tested on ToxiBench, obtaining AUROC 0.82. Haddad et al. (2025) [V0066] applied the same approach to CellLife, yielding MAE 0.75. A fifth paper, Duarte et al. (2021) [V0050], investigates fraudulent transaction detection with message‑passing relational graphs; it does not employ a Bayesian hierarchical model and is included only for completeness.",
